  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of State obligated $5.1B on federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 47.8% year over year. The agency awarded 17,054 contracts so far, with an average award size of $302K. Fiscal-year comparisons show a decline from prior peaks: FY21 was $9.5B, FY22 was $11.9B, FY23 was $11.7B, FY24 was $11.7B, and FY25 was $9.9B. Contract spending concentration is visible by industry and vendor: Security Guards and Patrol Services accounted for $794M, Other Computer Related Services accounted for $655M, and Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $551M. On the vendor side, CGI FEDERAL INC. received $181M, CITIBANK, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION received $159M, and INTER-CON SECURITY SYSTEMS, INC. received $148M. The FY2026 to date totals are partial, fiscal year to date, so the figures represent obligations recorded so far in the fiscal year rather than a full-year total.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 contract spending compare to recent years?",
        "body": "The Department of State obligated $5.1B in FY2026 to date, down 47.8% year over year. FY25 obligations were $9.9B, and FY24 obligations were $11.7B. FY22 obligations peaked at $11.9B in the five-year span shown."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the top goods and services and who gets the work?",
        "body": "Security Guards and Patrol Services leads NAICS categories at $794M, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $655M and Computer Systems Design Services at $551M. CGI FEDERAL INC. is the top vendor at $181M, followed by CITIBANK, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION at $159M and INTER-CON SECURITY SYSTEMS, INC. at $148M. The top ten vendors together include banks, IT services, and security firms, reflecting the agency mix of financial, technical, and protective needs."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of State spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of State obligated $5.1B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The agency recorded 17,054 awards with an average award size of $302K. Obligations fell 47.8% year over year, and prior-year totals include $9.9B in FY25 and $11.7B in FY24."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does State buy?",
      "a": "State buys security, IT, and professional services. Security Guards and Patrol Services accounted for $794M, Other Computer Related Services accounted for $655M, Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $551M, Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services accounted for $401M, and Facilities Support Services accounted for $296M in FY2026 to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are State's largest contractors?",
      "a": "State's largest contractors are CGI FEDERAL INC. ($181M), CITIBANK, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION ($159M), and INTER-CON SECURITY SYSTEMS, INC. ($148M). Other top vendors include TRIPLE CANOPY INC ($142M), MINBURN TECHNOLOGY GROUP, LLC ($140M), and GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. ($137M)."
    }
